+# Resident MiniCPM-V 4.7 35B-A3B LES server — M4 16 GB validation
+
+Date: 2026-10-14. Local-only worktree: `fix/les-openai-server`. Underlying LES `ios-omni` base: `96bbf61`.
+
+## Scope and implementation
+
+- Native C++ target: `llama-les-native-server`, optional `-DLLAMA_BUILD_LES_NATIVE_SERVER=ON` (default OFF).
+- Uses the fork's **current** `server_context`, `server_routes`, `server_http_context`; never modifies the LES backend, expert layout, models or their top-8 routing.
+- Routes exposed on loopback: `GET /health`, `GET /v1/models`, `POST /v1/chat/completions`, `POST /completion`, `POST /tokenize`, `GET /props`.
+- Model weight load once per native server process. Port tested `127.0.0.1:18793`; `--host 0.0.0.0` rejected **before loading weights**, process exit 2. Not externally authenticated.
+- Native CLI build on local Apple M4 Metal: **PASS**. Plain chat: HTTP 200. `tool_choice=required` produced a proper `message.tool_calls` object (run_tests), HTTP 200; initial tool request 273 prompt tokens, ~47.22 seconds without shared task prefix.
+
+## Cache mode
+
+Recommended tested config:
+
+```text
+--moe-slot-bank 128 -c 4096 -b 64 -ub 16 -ngl all -t 4 --parallel 1
+--reasoning off --reasoning-format none --jinja --swa-full --cache-prompt
+LLAMA_MOE_LOOKAHEAD_PREFETCH=0
+```
+
+SWA-full matters for this MoE hybrid context: without it the resident server emitted warnings about insufficient cache state and forced full prompt reprocessing. **After enabling `--swa-full`**, an *identical* 124-token chat request was 15.08 s (cached 0) and then 0.57 s (cached 107). These are successive cold/warm samples, NOT a scientifically controlled LES/SWA A/B comparison.
+
+## Real coding-agent workflow (native API + host-executed tools)
+
+- Sandbox: disposable copy of `agent-bench/tasks/session`.
+- Server's actual OpenAI-compatible `tool_calls`; host validates paths and only edits sandbox `source.py`.
+- Tool sequence: run_tests -> read_file -> read_file -> replace_text -> run_tests -> final.
+- Result: real edit to SessionRegistry.revoke, 6/6 independent unittest **PASS**. No code outside the sandbox was modified.
+- Total: **362.4 sec**, 6 model turns, 5 real tool calls. Cumulative swap **not observed increasing** (approx. 297.38 MB already in use). Not a measurement of all Metal/unified memory.
+
+| Assistant turn | HTTP request time | Prompt tokens | Cached tokens | Action |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| 0 | 87.15 s | 531 | 0 | run_tests (initial failure) |
+| 1 | 62.64 s | 882 | 494 | read_file |
+| 2 | 35.79 s | 1,026 | 862 | read_file |
+| 3 | 113.91 s | see JSON log | 862 | replace_text, applied |
+| 4 | 43.05 s | see JSON log | 1,279 | run_tests, 6/6 PASS |
+| 5 | 19.04 s | see JSON log | 1,542 | final summary |
+
+- Previous Python **process-per-turn** bridge session example: 555.3 sec, six turns, five calls but included a rejected tool call; tool trajectory differs. ~35% smaller wall clock **is illustrative, not strict apples-to-apples speedup**.
+- Agent source of truth: `/Volumes/ssd/les-eval/agent-bench/real_agent_native_session.json`; log: `real_agent_native_session_swa.log`.
+- Repeated-prefix cache artifacts: `cache_swa_full_1.json`, `cache_swa_full_2.json`; native smoke tests: `native_plain.json`, `native_tool.json`.
+- Native persistent server log: `native-swa-full.log`, includes restored context checkpoints.
+
+## Known limitations / next optimizations
+
+1. Hybrid/SWA model still has costly new-token prefill and SSD expert I/O; agent took minutes. `--swa-full` does NOT make every growing history an exact cache hit. Try normalized, shorter tool definitions and more compact tool results; benchmark one factor at a time.
+2. Current `--reasoning-format none` leaves literal empty `<think>` tags in content for short replies, though native tool call parsing was correct. Avoid treating the endpoint as fully spec-compliant without more request/streaming/error tests.
+3. Context capacity in real agent test was 4,096; 8K/16K native persistent context and sustained concurrency on this 16GB Mac were not tested. Monitor memory pressure and swap before raising.
+4. Native server has a minimal route set and no external auth, TLS, sandboxed tools or graceful admin shutdown. Keep it strictly loopback and use an allowlisted host agent to execute tool calls.
+5. Cache timing is affected by SSD/macOS page cache and the workload. For a high-frequency **text-only Coding Agent** on this same M4, the previously benchmarked Qwen REAP48 remains the more pragmatic default; MiniCPM 35B is interesting for multimodal capability and split-expert inference.
