+## Native resident LES server (preferred, experimental)
+
+The optional native HTTP target reuses the current `server_context` and `server_http_context` APIs instead of the old incompatible `tools/server/server.cpp`:
+
+```bash
+cmake -S . -B /Volumes/ssd/les-eval/build \
+  -DGGML_METAL=ON -DGGML_ACCELERATE=ON \
+  -DLLAMA_BUILD_LES_NATIVE_SERVER=ON
+cmake --build /Volumes/ssd/les-eval/build --target llama-les-native-server -j 4
+
+LLAMA_MOE_LOOKAHEAD_PREFETCH=0 \
+/Volumes/ssd/les-eval/build/bin/llama-les-native-server \
+  -m /Volumes/ssd/les-eval/models/35B-A3B/MiniCPM-V-4_7-35B-A3B-mix_q3gud_im-les.gguf \
+  --moe-experts /Volumes/ssd/les-eval/models/35B-A3B/experts \
+  --moe-slot-bank 128 -c 4096 -b 64 -ub 16 -ngl all -t 4 \
+  --host 127.0.0.1 --port 18793 --parallel 1 \
+  --jinja --reasoning off --reasoning-format none \
+  --swa-full --cache-prompt
+```
+
+- `GET /health`, `GET /v1/models`, `POST /v1/chat/completions` (native OpenAI tool calls, including `tool_choice=required`), `POST /completion`, `POST /tokenize`, and `GET /props` are registered.
+- The backend and weights stay resident; unlike the Python bridge, it can reuse KV context between calls.
+- **Important:** this hybrid/SWA model did not retain reusable prompt KV without `--swa-full`. An identical 124-token request repeated with `--swa-full` showed `cached_tokens` 0 → 107 and duration 15.08s → 0.57s. This is an exact-repeat cache test, **not** an estimate of real Agent latency or end-to-end quality.
+- `--swa-full` increases KV memory requirements. Start with one server slot and 4096 context on 16GB; monitor swap and memory pressure when scaling context.
+- The current model/chat template may include literal `<think>...</think>` tags in `message.content` when using `--reasoning-format none`; consumers should account for that when showing responses.
+- The optional native target is loopback-only. Do not expose to the public network without adding authentication, resource limits and hardening.
+- The native frontend CMake target links the existing UI support library, which may trigger first-time frontend asset provisioning during a clean build.
+
+Native measurements live in `/Volumes/ssd/les-eval/agent-bench/native_*.json` and `native-swa-full.log`; do not mix them with the legacy process-per-turn bridge measurements.
